---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site.config';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description={`The terms governing use of ${SITE.name} — acceptable use, intellectual property, disclaimers and limitation of liability.`}
  lede="The rules for using this site."
  lastUpdated={new Date('2026-08-02')}
>
  <div class="not-prose mb-8 rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-warning)]/40 bg-[var(--color-warning)]/10 p-4 text-sm text-[var(--text-muted)]">
    <strong class="text-[var(--text)]">Template notice:</strong> these terms are a
    good-faith starting point, not legal advice. Have them reviewed by a qualified
    practitioner in your jurisdiction before relying on them.
  </div>

  <h2>1. Acceptance</h2>
  <p>
    By accessing <strong>{SITE.domain}</strong> you agree to these terms. If you do not
    agree, do not use the site.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Purpose of the content</h2>
  <p>
    All content is published for <strong>educational and defensive security purposes</strong>.
    It is general information, not professional security, legal or financial advice, and it
    is not a substitute for an assessment of your own environment by a qualified
    practitioner.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>You agree not to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Use anything published here to access, test or interfere with systems you do not own
      or lack written authorisation to test. Unauthorised access is a criminal offence in
      most jurisdictions.
    </li>
    <li>Scrape, mirror or bulk-republish the content without permission.</li>
    <li>Attempt to disrupt, overload or compromise the site or its infrastructure.</li>
    <li>Misrepresent the content as your own or as an endorsement of your product.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    Articles, artwork and site design are &copy; {new Date().getFullYear()}
    {' '}{SITE.organization.legalName} unless stated otherwise. You may quote short extracts
    with clear attribution and a link to the source article. Republishing whole articles
    requires written permission.
  </p>
  <p>
    Code samples published in articles may be used freely in your own projects. Third-party
    trademarks referenced remain the property of their owners; their use here is nominative
    and does not imply endorsement.
  </p>

  <h2>5. External links</h2>
  <p>
    We link to third-party resources where they are useful. We do not control them and are
    not responsible for their content, accuracy or security.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Availability</h2>
  <p>
    The site is provided "as is" and "as available". We do not guarantee uninterrupted
    access, and we may change, suspend or remove content at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
  <p>
    To the maximum extent permitted by law, we disclaim all warranties, express or implied,
    including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement. See
    the full <a href="/disclaimer">disclaimer</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the maximum extent permitted by law, {SITE.organization.legalName} is not liable for
    any indirect, incidental, consequential or punitive damages, or for any loss of data,
    profits or business, arising from your use of this site or reliance on its content.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms. Continued use after a change constitutes acceptance of the
    revised terms.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms:
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.organization.email}`}>{SITE.organization.email}</a>.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
